From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: djvalic <djvalic@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 12:37:35 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] wizard: filament put into the IFS no longer hides the setup
 wizard

Found on Kiln OS v1.0.0-rc7: a filament came out of the IFS during the
setup wizard's IFS tuning, and the user put it back. The port's sensor
went from empty to present, so FilamentInsertWatcher opened the slot
editor (filament/auto_open_editor; each IFS port is a prep sensor since
patch 0004) over the wizard: should_open_editor_on_insert() had no
wizard guard. Closing the editor called nav::go_back(), whose
stale-overlay sweep hides every screen child that is not the app
layout, a backdrop, chrome or a panel in the stack. The wizard's
container is none of those, so it was hidden, and Home showed. The
wizard stayed active (is_wizard_active()), so Settings > Printer > Run
Setup Wizard returned without doing anything, and only a restart got
the wizard back. A panel switch (a navbar tap with an overlay open) has
the same sweep.

Three changes:
- FilamentInsertContext gets wizard_active, and the policy opens no
  editor while it is set. The watcher fills it with the gate the boot
  loader notice uses: Config::is_wizard_required() || is_wizard_active().
  The lane baselines still move, so a spool put in under the wizard is
  what is loaded afterwards, not a late insert. The wizard's own steps
  ask for filament (the AD5X filament step sets the materials).
- ui_effects gets one "kept screen layer" (set_kept_screen_layer(),
  is_kept_screen_layer(), cleared when the object is deleted), and both
  sweeps in ui_nav_manager.cpp leave it alone. The wizard registers its
  container when it creates it and clears it when it goes. Unlike chrome
  it is not raised over overlays: an overlay opened over the wizard
  still covers it until it closes.
- ui_wizard_reshow() shows a hidden wizard container again and puts it
  in front. Settings' Run Setup Wizard and purge box rows call it while
  a wizard is active, instead of returning silently.

Tests: the insert policy's "every guard suppresses" gets a "setup wizard
open" section; a watcher test (an untagged insert with wizard_active
opens nothing and claims no prompt, and is no insert afterwards);
nav tests with a screen child standing in for the wizard (kept after
push_overlay + go_back and after a navbar switch, hidden as before when
not kept, no longer kept once deleted); the wizard's container is kept,
and ui_wizard_reshow() shows and raises it.
